//! `@derive(Identity)` — A NODE'S CONTENT IDENTITY, read off the node
//! model: a tag, the type's name, then one folded value per payload.
//! Spans never participate, so reformatting never changes an identity,
//! and two nodes with the same content wear the same number however
//! far apart they sit in the arena.
//!
//! EACH NODE RECORD DERIVES ITS OWN `identity`: a `collect enum E:
//! Identity` implements the trait over its members and reaches the
//! member's impl, so no arm per variant is written here.
//!
//! IT IS NOT `Fingerprint`, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS NOT COSMETIC.
//! `Fingerprint` folds a VALUE's own fields. A node's payloads are
//! `ExprId`s — `{ index: int }` — so folding the value folds an ARENA
//! POSITION, and two structurally identical subtrees would wear
//! different identities, which is the one thing a fingerprint must
//! never do. A node's identity is only meaningful THROUGH its arena,
//! so `identity` takes the arena and an id payload reaches its answer
//! through the store's memoized column.
//!
//! THE FOLD ITSELF IS `Fingerprint`'S, CALLED AND NEVER COPIED.
//! `parted` writes the tag and folds the type's name at derive time —
//! one fold, one literal tag, in the one file `make fingerprints` can
//! read it in. What THIS derive owns is the row per payload TYPE.
//!
//! A PARTS LIST IS FIXED ARITY. Every variable-length payload folds
//! through `fp_list` to ONE value before it stands in a parts list, so
//! no payload's boundary can move and two shapes cannot splice to one
//! sequence.
//!
//! It stands ALONE in this file on purpose (CLAUDE.md).
use @std.meta.{Type as MetaType, Declared, Directive, Code}

/// The compiler's derive for a node's content identity.
export trait Identity {
    fn identity(arena: SyntaxArena) -> int

    /// `@local` and `@facet` fields are not part of what a node folds.
    static fn marks(t: MetaType) -> List<string> { [local_word, facet_word] }

    static fn derive(t: MetaType) -> List<Directive> {
        [
            Directive {
                twin: "",
                name: t.name,
                at: t.at,
                source: quote {
                    impl Identity for ${t} {
                        fn identity(arena: SyntaxArena) -> int { ${folding(t, identity_of)} }
                    }
                },
            },
        ]
    }
}

/// A named payload folds by its own `identity`.
fn identity_of(e: Code) -> Code { quote { ${e}.identity(arena) } }
